'''Jek Lawquane''' was a [[Gender|male]] [[human/Twi'lek hybrid]] who was the son of [[Suu Lawquane]] and the adopted son of [[Cut Lawquane]] during the [[Clone Wars]].<ref name="TD" />

==Biography==
===Early life===
Jek Lawquane was [[Reproduction|born]] in [[25 BBY]]<ref name="Age" /> to [[Suu Lawquane]]<ref name="TD" /> and [[Suu Lawquane's spouse]].<ref name="Sanctuary" /> At some point after the [[First Battle of Geonosis|Battle of Geonosis]] during the [[Clone Wars]], Jek and his sister, [[Shaeeah Lawquane]], gained a<ref name="TD" /> stepfather<ref name="The Deserter classic guide">{{SWArchive|url=theclonewars/guide/episode210.html|text=''The Clone Wars'' Episode Guide: The Deserter}}</ref> when Suu married [[Cut Lawquane|Cut]], a former [[clone trooper]] who had abandoned the fighting after [[Attack on a Republic troop transport|losing]] his team. The [[Lawquane family|Lawquanes]] lived as [[farmer]]s on the [[planet]] [[Saleucami]].<ref name="TD" />

===The Clone Wars===
[[File:JekLawquane-TCWs2BR.png|thumb|left|160px|Jek during the Clone Wars]]
In [[21 BBY]], [[Clone Captain]] [[Rex]] was injured during the [[Battle of Saleucami]] while on a patrol. [[Cloning|Clone]] troopers [[Jesse]], [[Kix]] and [[Hardcase]] brought him to the [[Lawquane's Farm|Lawquane farm]] to recover as it was nearby. Despite misgivings about clones, Suu allowed Rex to spend the night at the farm, although she attempted to keep her children away from the [[soldier]]s. While playing in the field surrounding their house, Jek and Shaeeah stumbled across a Separatist escape pod left from the [[Battle of Saleucami]] overhead. While exploring the escape pod, Shaeeah accidentally pushed a button, activating [[BX-series droid commando|commando droids]] that were stored inside. Shaeeah and Jek fled back to their house, where their father fought off the droids with the help of Captain Rex. When Rex recovered and left, he decided not to report Cut Lawquane as a deserter to the Republic, allowing Jek to stay with his adoptive father.<ref name="TD" />

At a point later in the Clone Wars, the Lawquanes made the acquaintance of the irregular [[clone commando]] squad [[Clone Force 99]], nicknamed the Bad Batch, who also chose not to report Cut for desertion.<ref name="Cut and Run">{{TBB|Cut and Run}}</ref>

===Imperial Era===
After the end of the war and [[Proclamation of the New Order|rise]] of the [[Galactic Empire]] in [[19 BBY]],<ref name="Galactic Atlas">''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]''</ref> the Lawquanes decided to leave Saleucami after Rex,<ref name="Cut and Run" /> now a fugitive after having his [[behavioral modification biochip]] removed,<ref name="Shattered">{{TCW|Shattered}}</ref> stopped by their farm and warned them about the rising Empire and told them about the chips. The day afterwards, the Bad Batch, who had also deserted the Empire, arrived on Saleucami. Jek and Shaeeah ran into the house to see the new arrivals, and after being greeted by [[Wrecker]], were introduced to [[Echo]], who had joined the squad more recently, and [[Omega]], a child clone who had come with the Batch when they [[Escape from Kamino|escaped]] [[Kamino]]. The two children insisted that Omega come play with them.<ref name="Cut and Run" />

===Legacy===
{{Quote|You know the Lawquanes? Old man Cut, he fought in the Clone Wars. He saw the truth of things: No side in war is the right side. He did the right thing. Settled down. Had a family. Never got drawn back into the muck.|Glen Taffral, to his children|<ref name="Aftermath">[[Aftermath (novel)|''Aftermath'']]</ref>}}
In [[4 ABY]],<ref name="4 ABY">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates the events of ''Aftermath'' to [[4 ABY]].</ref> [[Glen Taffral]], a man to lived on Saleucami with his sons, [[Dav Taffral|Dav]] and [[Webb Taffral]], who each served opposing sides in the [[Galactic Civil War]], mentioned the Lawquane family in a lesson for his bickering children. Using Cut Lawquane and his family as examples, Glen instructed his sons to put aside their ideological differences and choose to stick by family over government, as Cut did during the Clone Wars.<ref name="Aftermath" />

==Personality and traits==
Jek Lawquane was a male<ref name="TD" /> [[human]]-[[Twi'lek]] [[hybrid]], who was 0.95 [[meter]]s, or 3 [[Foot|feet]], 1 inch tall,<ref name="Join the Battle" /> with [[Color|brown]] [[eye]]s and tan skin.<ref name="TD" /> Jek did his chores and enjoyed drawing pictures of people and places he could only imagine. The Clone Wars dividing the galaxy seemed to have nothing to do with him and was not a concern, until he and Shaeeah accidentally activated several commando droids.<ref name="Join the Battle" />

==Skills and abilities==
Like his parents and sister, Jek was a farmer.<ref name="Join the Battle" />

==Behind the scenes==
Jek's first appearance was in the TV series [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars|''Star Wars: The Clone Wars'''s]] [[2010]] episode [[The Deserter]], where he was voiced by [[Kath Soucie]]. In the subtitles for the episode, Jek's name is misspelled as "Jekk." [[Pablo Hidalgo]] mentioned Jek was always intended to have a human father, although they are not Cut's children.<ref name="Twitter">{{Twitter|pablohidalgo|status/703719160757383168|[[Pablo Hidalgo]]|date=2016-02-27|quote=They're not Cut's children, biologically, but they did have a human father. [...] It wasn't said, but it was part of their character design.|archivefile=File:PabloHidalgo-CutsChildren-Twitter.jpg|nolive=1}}</ref> Concept art for ''The Clone Wars'' of Jek and Shaeeah in the background behind Suu was done by [[Wayne Lo]].<ref name="Art of TCW">''[[The Art of Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''</ref> Jek's model was designed by [[Darren Marshall]] and finished on [[May 14]], [[2008]].<ref name="Deserter EG">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/the-deserter-episode-guide|text="The Deserter" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref>

